    <!-- Comprehensive Step-by-Step How-To Guide -->
    <string name="howto_title">How to Pair &amp; Use (Step-by-Step)</string>
    <string name="howto_subtitle">Works with Medtronic MiniMed 780G, 770G and 680G via Bluetooth LE</string>

    <string name="howto_step1_title">Prepare your MiniMed pump</string>
    <string
    name="howto_step1_desc"
  >On your pump, open: Menu → Settings → Device Settings → Mobile Devices.\nImportant: A pump can only talk to ONE phone at a time. If it was paired with MiniMed Mobile before, delete the old phone on the pump and uninstall/stop the official app.</string>

    <string name="howto_step2_title">Start pairing in this app</string>
    <string
    name="howto_step2_desc"
  >Tap "Pair New Pump" above. Your phone will start broadcasting as a Bluetooth LE peripheral named Mobile … (the app shows the exact name, for example Mobile 123456).</string>

    <string name="howto_step3_title">Confirm on the pump screen</string>
    <string
    name="howto_step3_desc"
  >On the pump, select "Pair New Device", wait until it finds the Mobile … name shown in the app and confirm. When the phone shows the Bluetooth pairing request, tap Pair. The encrypted SAKE handshake takes 5 to 10 seconds. Once connected, readings update every 15 seconds.</string>

    <string name="howto_step4_title">Keep background monitoring alive 24/7</string>
    <string
    name="howto_step4_desc"
  >Phones like Xiaomi, Realme, OPPO, Samsung or Huawei may kill background Bluetooth apps when the screen is off. Disable battery optimization for MGlycemia to ensure uninterrupted night alerts.</string>
    <string name="btn_battery_settings">Open Battery Optimization Settings</string>

    <string name="faq_title">FAQ &amp; Troubleshooting</string>
    <string
    name="faq_body"
  >• Supported pumps: MiniMed 780G (MMT-1886, verified), 770G and 680G.\n• Older pumps (640G, Veo, Paradigm): Use sub-GHz radio, not Bluetooth, so they cannot connect directly to a phone without a hardware bridge.\n• If pairing fails: Delete the Mobile … entry from the pump\'s Mobile Devices list, toggle Bluetooth off and on again on the phone, and tap "Pair New Pump".\n• Safety guarantee: This app is 100% READ-ONLY. It cannot deliver boluses, change basal rates, or alter any pump setting.</string>

